# demo-video fake-agent cassette — Claude Code TUI for the README hero cut (Issue #2381)
#
# Format: <delayMs>|@input|@exec|@transcript|@hook|@pass <TAB> <payload>
#   - payload is expanded with `printf %b` (\e, \n, \t, \\)
#   - `{{INPUT}}` / `{{TASK}}` are the message CommandMate sent; `{{WORKTREE}}`
#     is --worktree
#
# Two passes, in the order storyboard/readme-hero.yaml sends them:
#
#   1. The delegation round trip — claude-delegate.cast, row for row. `@exec`
#      REALLY runs `commandmate ask … --instance codex … --json` in the pane, so
#      the product's send → wait → History path runs unchanged; the codex pane
#      is codex-review.cast. `@transcript` appends transcripts/claude-delegate.jsonl
#      before the ready frame; `@hook` reports both ends of the turn.
#   2. An approval — the frames of claude-session-sample.cast (Reading the
#      header, `⏺ Bash(npm run test:unit)`, `Do you want to proceed?` with
#      `❯ 1. Yes`), minus its Editing rows, because this pass runs the tests
#      rather than making the change. The `@pass` row in front of it clears
#      `{{TASK}}`, so the pass echoes ITS instruction and not the delegation's.
#      The second `@input` is the answer the phone sends; the frames after it
#      keep echoing `{{TASK}}`, the original instruction. `@transcript` appends
#      transcripts/claude-tests.jsonl, whose reply links Header.tsx so the phone
#      has a link to tap.
#
# The cut's order matters: storyboard.ts refuses a cut that places the
# file-link or approval scenes before `delegate-ask`, because pass 2 is only
# reachable after pass 1 (fake-agent.sh reads a cassette top to bottom and
# loops back to the banner when it runs out).
#
# Provenance: every frame is a real `tmux capture-pane` capture of a Claude Code
# session, sanitised — see claude-session-sample.cast's header — with the
# detector's anchors verbatim:
#   running -> "esc to interrupt" (CLAUDE_INTERRUPT_HINT_PATTERN) and the
#              spinner+U+2026 line (CLAUDE_THINKING_PATTERN)
#   ready   -> a line starting with U+276F (CLAUDE_PROMPT_PATTERN) plus a
#              200-char U+2500 separator (CLAUDE_SEPARATOR_PATTERN)
#   waiting -> "Do you want to proceed?" over "❯ 1. Yes" / "2. No, …"
#              (detectMultipleChoicePrompt; option 1 pre-selected)
# Stripping the ANSI or shortening the separator breaks real detection, so do
# not "tidy" this file. Both reply frames are held 8 s after `Stop`, so the loop
# back to the banner lands after the poller's 5 s capture cache saw them.
#
# The running frame of pass 1 is on screen for the whole `@exec` (however long
# codex takes), and the `ask` output lands BELOW it for the instant before the
# next row repaints — keep the running anchors within the last 15 lines of the
# frame above the tool row, as here, so a capture taken in that instant still
# reads as running.

